# Training data and model files (too large for git — ~600MB of MRI scans).
# Stripped from history with git-filter-repo; keep them out of the repo.
#
# The exception is the model provenance records: the training, calibration,
# OOD, verification and fairness JSON beside each artifact. They are a few
# kilobytes each, they are what every model card and every published figure is
# built from, and leaving them untracked meant a correction to a model's record
# survived only on one machine. The reason for this rule is size; these are not
# large. Weights (*.h5), arrays (*.npz) and the imaging itself stay out.
dataset/*
!dataset/data/
dataset/data/*
!dataset/data/*.json
# Except these two, which are only meaningful beside data that stays ignored.
# skin_tone_performance.json records a measurement of a specific .h5, and
# ita_reference.json is a reference distribution over specific test images.
# Tracking them without those files puts a checkout in a state no environment
# should be in: tests/fairness.test.ts uses their presence as the signal that
# the data is here, so committing them made CI run assertions against an
# artifact it does not have (measured fingerprint ed06b8a0468e against a null
# deployed one) instead of skipping. They are backed up by
# `npm run backup:models`, like the artifacts they describe.
dataset/data/skin_tone_performance.json
dataset/data/ita_reference.json
!dataset/lung_cancer_MRI_dataset/
dataset/lung_cancer_MRI_dataset/*
!dataset/lung_cancer_MRI_dataset/*.json
!dataset/lung_nodule_model/
dataset/lung_nodule_model/*
!dataset/lung_nodule_model/*.json
*.h5
*.pkl
*.joblib

# Uploads
uploads/
temp/
